From 30a2082e6ee61d13210e5b5c3f6cea79a74350e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jonathan D.A. Jewell" <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:06:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(lock): guard leaf pin representation and ref
 provenance

GitHub rejects a leaf actions.lock record whose ref repeats its own 40-hex pin at
runner setup ("invalid lockfile pin") for every caller pinned to that commit.
The repair for the class landed on main in f335165 (#1271) and cf8f912 (#1285);
this adds the guard that fails on the shape before a commit becomes pinnable, for
records a workflow uses and for records it does not.

check-lock-pin-provenance.sh checks representation and, with --remote, ref
provenance. It deliberately does NOT re-implement coverage (check-lock-sync.sh)
or closure (close-lock.sh --check): a representation pass is not a statement
that a commit is safe to pin. Exit 2 whenever inspection did not happen.

Tests: 18 fixture cases, including the historical fad242d record shape (fails)
and the corrected 1725beb shape (passes).
